00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:20,890
Now in the forums,
在论坛中，

250
00:13:20,890 --> 00:13:24,090
one of the participants has mentioned
有一位学员提出了

251
00:13:24,090 --> 00:13:25,370
a very interesting point,
一个非常有意思的观点，

252
00:13:25,370 --> 00:13:28,570
which I've incorporated into my slides.
我已经把它放进了我的幻灯片。

253
00:13:28,570 --> 00:13:31,330
They have asked about selection of the site
他们问到了从环境风险的角度

254
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:34,550
in terms of the risk to the environment.
如何选址。

255
00:13:34,550 --> 00:13:38,450
Now BSL3 or a BSL4 facility
BSL3或BSL4设施

256
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:43,450
is a very expensive facility to build and operate.
的建造和运行都非常昂贵。

257
00:13:43,690 --> 00:13:47,270
So ideally it should be located in a site
所以理想情况下，它应该选在

258
00:13:47,270 --> 00:13:50,010
in which there is a low risk of natural disasters,
自然灾害风险较低的地点，

259
00:13:50,010 --> 00:13:52,250
such as earthquakes, flooding,
比如地震、洪水，

260
00:13:52,250 --> 00:13:55,550
or other tsunamis for instance.
或者其他如海啸等灾害。

261
00:13:55,550 --> 00:13:58,690
And it should be located in an area
它应该选在

262
00:13:58,690 --> 00:14:00,970
with a low population density,
人口密度较低的地区，

263
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:05,530
not in a centralized place such as a city.
而不是城市这样的中心地带。

264
00:14:05,530 --> 00:14:08,970
It should have access to electricity and water,
它应该能获得电力和水，

265
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:11,450
as these are critical components.
因为这些是关键要素。

266
00:14:11,450 --> 00:14:15,090
And in case of contingencies or emergencies,
在发生意外或紧急情况时，

267
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:19,470
the facility should be accessible to the hazmat teams,
危险品处置队应该能够进入该设施，

268
00:14:19,470 --> 00:14:21,610
which may involve personnel
其中可能包括

269
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:24,210
who has been specially trained
经过专门培训、

270
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:29,210
to manage spills and other risks associated
能处理溢洒及与生物因子相关的

271
00:14:30,090 --> 00:14:31,490
with biological agents.
其他风险的人员。

272
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:35,170
Generally each country has a hazmat team,
一般每个国家都有危险品处置队，

273
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:37,290
and these hazmat teams are deployed
这些队伍会在

274
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:40,130
in the event of a breach of containment.
发生防护失效时出动。

275
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:43,530
They consist of specialized personnel
他们由专业人员

276
00:14:43,530 --> 00:14:47,350
or specialists who are trained to manage chemical
或专家组成，受过处理化学品

277
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:49,810
as well as biological spills.
以及生物溢洒的培训。

278
00:14:49,810 --> 00:14:51,290
And as far as possible,
而且，请尽可能

279
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:54,290
please do not site your facility in a conflict zone
不要把你的设施建在冲突地区，

280
00:14:54,290 --> 00:14:58,410
in which there is a potential for war
也就是可能发生战争

281
00:14:59,330 --> 00:15:00,850
or terrorism.
或恐怖主义的地方。

282
00:15:00,850 --> 00:15:03,250
These are some of the issues
这些是选址时

283
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:08,900
which must be addressed when selecting a site.
必须解决的一些问题。

284
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:13,480
Now, one of the key factors or the key elements
保护实验室使用者和环境的

285
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:16,200
which protects the laboratory user and the environment
一个关键因素或关键要素

286
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,880
is directional air flow.
是定向气流。

287
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:21,200
And I will explain this to you in a diagram
在这一讲中，我会用一张图

288
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,560
during the course of this lecture.
向大家解释这一点。

289
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:29,520
So air is basically fluid and it can be pressurized
空气本质上是流体，它可以被加压，

290
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:32,000
and this makes it an indispensable agent
这使它成为

291
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,840
for the containment of biological agents.
生物因子防护中不可或缺的要素。

292
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,600
Generally facilities are designed
一般来说，设施的设计

293
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:40,000
so that the air flows from the clean to the dirty zones
是让空气从清洁区流向污染区，

294
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:43,840
prior to release into the environment
然后经过HEPA过滤器

295
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:47,720
via the HEPA filters.
再排放到环境中。

296
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,720
Let us look at this concept of clean and dirty.
让我们来看看清洁和污染这个概念。

297
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:54,040
Now this is your laboratory worker
这是实验室工作人员，

298
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:56,560
and this is the biological agent.
这是生物因子。

299
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:59,680
Now, if there is a directional air flow
如果定向气流

300
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:04,160
moving from this side towards the laboratory worker,
是从这一侧流向实验室工作人员，

301
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:05,760
this is not acceptable.
这是不可接受的。

302
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:09,920
As any aerosol generated by this biological agent
因为这个生物因子在移液、离心等操作中

303
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,480
during operations such as pipetting and centrifugation
产生的任何气溶胶

304
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:15,400
will be blown directly towards the laboratory worker.
都会被直接吹向实验室工作人员。

305
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:18,420
And this will pose a risk to the laboratory worker.
这会对实验室工作人员构成风险。

306
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:22,920
Directional air flow ensures that the air flows
定向气流确保空气

307
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:23,760
from this side.
从这一侧流动。

308
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:28,760
So you have your HEPA filtered air flowing via baffles
经HEPA过滤的空气通过导流板流入，

309
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:32,880
or you can imagine this like an air conditioning vent
你可以把它想象成空调出风口，

310
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:36,340
but only in the case of BSL two and three,
只不过在BSL2和BSL3的情况下，

311
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:39,200
the air is actually filtered
空气实际上是经过过滤的，

312
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:43,240
and this air generally flows over the laboratory worker
这些空气一般会流过实验室工作人员，

313
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:46,080
and it exits from the other end of the facility
然后从设施的另一端排出，

314
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:49,200
also via a HEPA filter.
同样要经过HEPA过滤器。

315
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:52,480
So this is the concept of directional air flow.
这就是定向气流的概念。

316
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:54,440
So that's the exit of the dirty air.
这里是污染空气的出口。

317
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:56,680
So this area is generally designated as clean
这个区域一般被划定为清洁区，

318
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:59,360
and this area is designated as dirty.
这个区域被划定为污染区。

319
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:01,000
So in the case of a spill, for instance,
例如，如果发生溢洒，

320
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,280
you spill this biological agent on the floor over here,
比如你把这个生物因子洒在了这里的地板上，

321
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:08,360
your cleanup should be done from this direction.
清理应该从这个方向进行。

322
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:12,200
Do not step into this area and try to clean up the spill.
不要踏进这个区域去清理溢洒物。

323
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,400
You try and clean up from the other side.
要尽量从另一侧进行清理。

324
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:19,640
I will discuss this in spill cleanups.
我会在讲溢洒清理时讨论这一点。

325
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,320
Now, another important aspect about air
关于空气的另一个重要方面

326
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:27,320
is it has fluidity and we can pressurize it
是它具有流动性，我们可以对它加压，

327
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:31,520
or you can generate negative pressure.
也可以产生负压。

328
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,880
So a containment facility is maintained
防护设施

329
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:35,520
at a negative pressure with reference
相对于外部环境

330
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,240
to the external environment.
保持负压状态。

331
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:40,160
This ensures that aerosols containing biological agents
这确保含有生物因子的气溶胶

332
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:45,630
are contained within the negative pressure zone.
被控制在负压区域内。

333
00:17:45,630 --> 00:17:48,030
Okay, now one of the procedures
好，我们产生气溶胶的

334
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:50,790
we generate aerosols is pipetting.
一种操作是移液。

335
00:17:50,790 --> 00:17:52,830
Another one is centrifugation
另一种是离心，

336
00:17:52,830 --> 00:17:56,750
and these aerosols are generated within a facility
这些气溶胶是在设施内产生的，

337
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:58,390
and the purpose of the PPE
而个人防护装备，

338
00:17:58,390 --> 00:17:59,950
or personal protective equipment
也就是PPE的作用，

339
00:17:59,950 --> 00:18:01,910
is to protect the laboratory worker
是保护实验室工作人员

340
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:04,590
or the laboratory user from the aerosols.
或实验室使用者免受气溶胶的危害。

341
00:18:04,590 --> 00:18:09,590
However, aerosols can be generated at a very high load
但是，气溶胶可能以非常高的浓度产生，

342
00:18:10,390 --> 00:18:14,310
and this is why we need to constantly circulate air
这就是为什么我们需要让空气

343
00:18:14,310 --> 00:18:15,590
through this facility.
在这个设施中不断循环。

344
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:20,590
So the air circulation serves like a washing system.
空气循环就像一个清洗系统。

345
00:18:20,950 --> 00:18:22,790
It washes through the facility.
它把整个设施冲洗一遍。

346
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:25,230
Imagine you have used a detergent on your clothes
想象一下，你在衣服上用了洗涤剂，

347
00:18:25,230 --> 00:18:27,190
and you wash it multiple times
你要洗好几遍，

348
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,470
until the detergent moves away.
直到把洗涤剂冲掉。

349
00:18:29,470 --> 00:18:30,750
This is a laundry procedure
这是洗衣的过程，

350
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:34,390
but the same analogy applies in this facility.
但同样的类比也适用于这个设施。

351
00:18:34,390 --> 00:18:36,470
So there's a constant flow of air
空气不断流动，

352
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:39,030
taking away the aerosols
把气溶胶带走，

353
00:18:39,030 --> 00:18:43,850
and filtering them out through the HEPA filter.
并通过HEPA过滤器把它们过滤掉。

354
00:18:43,850 --> 00:18:48,310
Okay, HEPA filters are built to certain standards.
好，HEPA过滤器是按照一定标准制造的。

355
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:51,250
So according to European standards,
根据欧洲标准，

356
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:55,250
a HEPA air filter must remove at least 99.95%
HEPA空气过滤器必须至少去除99.95%的

357
00:18:55,970 --> 00:19:00,970
of particles whose diameter is equal to 0.3 micron.
直径等于0.3微米的颗粒。

358
00:19:02,410 --> 00:19:08,020
Okay, so this is what a HEPA filter is designed to do.
好，这就是HEPA过滤器的设计用途。

359
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:09,940
Okay, now this is a HEPA filter
这是一个HEPA过滤器，

360
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,300
which is mounted in a special housing
安装在一个专用的外壳中，

361
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:17,220
and each HEPA filter is fitted onto the facility itself
每个HEPA过滤器都通过密封件

362
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:18,300
via a seal.
安装在设施上。

363
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,740
So air can only pass through this filter
这样空气只能通过这个过滤器，

364
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:22,280
and not through the seal.
而不能从密封处通过。

365
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:24,380
And when HEPA filters are generally changed,
一般更换HEPA过滤器时，

366
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:26,260
they have to be bagged in and bagged out.
必须采用袋进袋出的方式。

367
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:28,820
So you fit a big bag on this HEPA filter
你要在这个HEPA过滤器上套一个大袋子，

368
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:32,260
and this has to be done by specialized personnel
这必须由专业人员来做，

369
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,560
and the entire filter is bagged out
整个过滤器被装袋取出，

370
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:36,740
and then decontaminated
然后进行去污，

371
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:38,980
and you cannot reuse a HEPA filter.
HEPA过滤器不能重复使用。

372
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:40,540
It's generally disposed of.
一般会被废弃处置。

373
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:43,480
Now this all adds to the cost of the facility itself.
这些都会增加设施本身的成本。

374
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:48,540
Now HEPA filters work by trapping particles
HEPA过滤器的工作原理是把颗粒截留

375
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:49,420
within a matrix.
在基质中。

376
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:52,380
So they have a filter matrix and this is compressed.
它们有一层过滤基质，是压实的。

377
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:55,580
So particles are intercepted
颗粒会被拦截，

378
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:58,580
and if they contain viruses or bacteria
如果其中含有气溶胶化的病毒或细菌，

379
00:19:58,580 --> 00:20:01,220
in aerosolized form, they will be trapped.
它们就会被截留。

380
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:04,020
They impact these filters and they cannot pass through.
它们撞击这些过滤器，无法穿过。

381
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:07,060
So as a particle passes through,
当颗粒穿过时，

382
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:09,600
the velocity is generally reduced
速度一般会降低，

383
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:12,920
and this particle then gets trapped in this filter.
然后这个颗粒就被截留在过滤器中。

384
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,060
Now you will ask me what happens to particles
你们会问我，那小于0.3微米的颗粒

385
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:17,540
which are less than 0.3 micron
会怎样呢？

386
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:22,220
and because of the multiple layers in a HEPA filter,
由于HEPA过滤器有多层，

387
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:24,780
the particles are actually trapped
这些颗粒实际上会在

388
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:27,580
at any one of these levels
其中任何一层被截留，

389
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:31,140
and you have clean air coming out from this filter.
从这个过滤器出来的就是洁净空气。

390
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:34,100
Now generally as HEPA filters age,
一般来说，随着HEPA过滤器老化，

391
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,960
they tend to become more efficient
它们往往会变得更高效，

392
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:38,040
as more and more particles are trapped
因为截留的颗粒越来越多，

393
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,700
but this does not mean the HEPA filter
但这并不意味着HEPA过滤器

394
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:41,020
should not be changed.
不需要更换。

395
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:43,700
You must change it as the matrix may degrade
你必须更换它，因为基质

396
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:51,340
over a period of time.
可能会随着时间推移而劣化。

397
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:53,500
We now move on to the facility design
现在我们来看建筑本身的

398
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,380
of the building itself.
设施设计。

399
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:56,420
Now this is a cross section of the facility.
这是设施的横截面。

400
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:57,900
It's a cross section view.
这是一个横截面视图。

401
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,340
So if you can imagine a facility,
如果你能想象一个设施，

402
00:21:00,340 --> 00:21:02,860
this one is the roof and this is the cross section.
这是屋顶，这是横截面。

403
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:06,560
Now a facility generally has a minimum of three floors.
一个设施一般至少有三层。

404
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,380
So the upper floor is a service floor
上层是设备服务层，

405
00:21:08,380 --> 00:21:10,900
which handles all the air,
负责处理所有空气，

406
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:14,460
your HEPA filters, compressors, pumps,
包括HEPA过滤器、压缩机、泵、

407
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,040
air conditioning equipment.
空调设备。

408
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:18,980
The lower floor or the floor which is in the basement
下层，也就是位于地下室的楼层，

409
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:23,200
handles the EDS or the effluent disposal system
负责EDS，即污水处置系统，

410
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:27,160
which traps all the liquid coming from the facility
它收集来自设施的所有液体，

411
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:31,280
including the liquid which comes after your shower.
包括淋浴后产生的液体。

412
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:36,280
And here the liquid is treated using chemical reagents
在这里，液体用化学试剂进行处理，

413
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:39,640
and finally disposed off to the system
最后排放到系统中，

414
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:43,180
which may involve your sewage system.
可能是排入污水系统。

415
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:47,080
You also have your administrative offices and laboratories.
还有行政办公室和实验室。

416
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:51,720
This is the design of the facility itself.
这就是设施本身的设计。

417
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:54,680
Now for laboratory design,
关于实验室设计，

418
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:56,720
this is a cross sectional view.
这是一个横截面视图。

419
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:59,160
We have our change areas in which we change
我们有更衣区，在这里我们

420
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:04,160
from our street clothes to our laboratory clothes
把日常便服换成实验室服装，

421
00:22:04,320 --> 00:22:07,240
which may involve or include PPEs
其中可能涉及或包括个人防护装备，

422
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:10,320
and we move to an airlock which is negative pressure
然后我们进入处于负压的气闸，

423
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:16,410
and then we move on to the containment laboratory.
再进入防护实验室。

424
00:22:16,410 --> 00:22:18,630
Now the service floors which are located
位于设施

425
00:22:18,630 --> 00:22:22,190
in the upper reaches of this facility
上部的设备服务层

426
00:22:22,190 --> 00:22:24,570
consist of the HEPA filters.
装有HEPA过滤器。

427
00:22:24,570 --> 00:22:26,190
Now these HEPA filters are designed
这些HEPA过滤器的设计

428
00:22:26,230 --> 00:22:29,710
so as to pump in clean air which protects the personnel
是为了泵入保护人员的洁净空气，

429
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:34,230
and then the dirty air or the contaminated air
然后污染的空气，也就是受污染的空气，

430
00:22:34,230 --> 00:22:36,270
is pumped out via HEPA filters
经HEPA过滤器泵出，

431
00:22:36,270 --> 00:22:38,730
before it is released into the environment.
再排放到环境中。

432
00:22:39,670 --> 00:22:43,750
Generally, there is something known as a strobic fan here
一般来说，这里有一种叫Strobic风机的设备，

433
00:22:43,750 --> 00:22:48,510
and this strobic fan resembles a jet engine, a turbine.
这种Strobic风机很像喷气发动机，像一台涡轮机。

434
00:22:48,510 --> 00:22:51,510
So these strobic fans are installed
这些Strobic风机安装在

435
00:22:51,510 --> 00:22:52,670
on the roof of the facility.
设施的屋顶上。

436
00:22:52,670 --> 00:22:55,150
They will pump the filtered air high
它们会把过滤后的空气高高地泵入

437
00:22:55,210 --> 00:22:56,670
into the environment.
环境中。

438
00:22:56,670 --> 00:22:58,270
So we'll have a plume which may go up
这样会形成一股烟羽，可能升到

439
00:22:58,270 --> 00:23:02,670
to 100 to 200 meters high and this dilutes the air
100到200米高，这会稀释空气，

440
00:23:02,670 --> 00:23:06,190
and reduces the likelihood of exposure
降低环境

441
00:23:06,190 --> 00:23:09,950
to the biological agent to the environment
和公众接触

442
00:23:09,950 --> 00:23:13,860
and the general public.
生物因子的可能性。

443
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:16,660
Now I have prepared a special video for you
我为大家准备了一段专门的视频，

444
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:20,380
in which I have walked through the service floors
在视频中我走遍了设备服务层，

445
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:23,580
and you can access this from your lecture notes.
你们可以从讲义中找到它。

446
00:23:23,580 --> 00:23:26,400
I have inserted a link in your PDF lecture notes.
我在PDF讲义中插入了一个链接。

447
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:33,560
You can click on the link and view this video.
你们可以点击链接观看这段视频。

448
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:36,560
This is what I have depicted in the video.
这就是我在视频中展示的内容。

449
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:39,000
Now these are the HEPA filters
这些是HEPA过滤器，

450
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,640
which are basically letting the air go out.
基本上是让空气排出去的。

451
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:42,920
So everything which exists,
所以所有排出

452
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:45,400
the facility passes through this HEPA filter.
设施的东西都要经过这个HEPA过滤器。

453
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:47,540
There are multiple filters inside this
这里面有多个过滤器，

454
00:23:47,540 --> 00:23:49,600
and as you can see, this is what is known
大家可以看到，这是所谓的

455
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:53,960
as a Magna-Helic gauge, which is a air pressure gauge
Magnehelic压差计，它是一种气压计，

456
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:58,120
and these are critical to monitoring of the system.
对系统监测至关重要。

457
00:23:58,120 --> 00:23:59,680
This is another HEPA filter.
这是另一个HEPA过滤器。

458
00:23:59,760 --> 00:24:03,120
This is the one in which air enters into the system
这是空气进入系统的那个，

459
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:05,280
and this HEPA filter is located directly
这个HEPA过滤器就位于

460
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:07,120
on top of the laboratory.
实验室正上方。

461
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:10,320
And these are the strobic fans.
这些是Strobic风机。

462
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:14,280
So the air from this particular HEPA filter
这个HEPA过滤器出来的空气

463
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:16,440
exits through this strobic fan.
通过这台Strobic风机排出。

464
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:17,920
It is pumped.
它是被泵出去的。

465
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:19,680
There's a turbine and it's pumped high
里面有一台涡轮机，把空气以气流形式

466
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:24,440
into the atmosphere in a stream and it's diluted.
高高地泵入大气中，使其稀释。

467
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:27,560
So in the case of a contingency or an emergency
所以在发生意外或紧急情况，

468
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:30,720
which involves compromising of this filter,
涉及这个过滤器失效时，

469
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:33,040
for example, there's a breakdown in this filter,
例如这个过滤器发生故障，

470
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:37,080
the strobic fan will still push or dilute the air
Strobic风机仍然会推送或稀释空气，

471
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:40,460
before it is released into the environment.
然后再排放到环境中。

472
00:24:40,460 --> 00:24:44,200
Generally, facilities are designed so as to shut down
一般来说，设施的设计是在

473
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:46,340
in the event of a breach of containment,
发生防护失效时关闭，

474
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:48,280
which means that everything shuts down
也就是说所有系统都关闭，

475
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:54,340
so nothing is released into the environment.
这样就不会有任何东西释放到环境中。

476
00:24:54,340 --> 00:24:56,500
Now with regard to effluent disposal,
关于污水处置，

477
00:24:56,500 --> 00:24:59,000
effluent refers to all the waste water
污水指的是来自设施的

478
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,840
coming from your facility.
所有废水。

479
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:04,000
This will include the waste water after your shower,
这包括淋浴后、

480
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,860
after hand washing, as well as from autoclaves.
洗手后以及高压灭菌器产生的废水。

481
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:10,000
All the waste water is directed to the basement
所有废水都被引到地下室，

482
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,200
in which there is a holding tank.
那里有一个储存罐。

483
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:15,520
This holding tank is designed to hold water
这个储存罐的设计容量

484
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:19,120
for at least a week's capacity of this laboratory.
至少能容纳这个实验室一周的废水量。

485
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:21,560
So in my particular laboratory,
在我的实验室，

486
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:25,600
our holding tank capacity is around 5,000 liters of water.
我们的储存罐容量约为5000升水。

487
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:28,360
From the holding tank, it is pumped
废水从储存罐被泵入

488
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,520
into the disinfection tank
消毒罐，

489
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:35,540
in which a decontaminate or a sterilizing agent is added.
在那里加入去污剂或灭菌剂。

490
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:37,840
This may be bleached.
这可能是漂白剂。

491
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,980
However, the SOP needs to be developed
不过，需要针对每种生物因子

492
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:43,840
for each biological agent.
制定标准操作程序。

493
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:48,640
After disinfection for the duration of the contact time,
在消毒达到接触时间后，

494
00:25:50,060 --> 00:25:55,060
the disinfected fluid is pumped into the neutralization tank
消毒后的液体被泵入中和罐，

495
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:59,620
where the disinfectant is neutralized prior to release.
在排放前把消毒剂中和掉。

496
00:25:59,620 --> 00:26:02,620
Now all these procedures must be monitored
所有这些程序都必须受到监控，

497
00:26:02,620 --> 00:26:05,300
and records must be maintained at all times
并且必须始终保存记录，

498
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:18,690
as part of the process of continuous quality improvement.
作为持续质量改进过程的一部分。

499
00:26:18,870 --> 00:26:20,530
We now move on to biosecurity
现在我们来谈生物安保，

500
00:26:20,530 --> 00:26:25,210
and facilities must be designed for biosecurity.
设施必须为生物安保而设计。

501
00:26:25,210 --> 00:26:28,290
And this must be implemented or incorporated
这必须落实或纳入

502
00:26:28,290 --> 00:26:30,450
into the building design.
建筑设计中。

503
00:26:30,450 --> 00:26:32,890
And this may include physical security
这可能包括以出入控制形式

504
00:26:32,890 --> 00:26:34,650
in the form of excess controls
实现的物理安保，

505
00:26:34,650 --> 00:26:37,810
as well as information security
以及信息安全

506
00:26:37,810 --> 00:26:43,590
or data security.
或数据安全。

507
00:26:43,590 --> 00:26:46,150
I will now move on to biological safety cabinet
现在我来讲生物安全柜，

508
00:26:46,150 --> 00:26:49,910
or what we call the BSC, biological safety cabinet.
也就是我们所说的BSC，生物安全柜。

509
00:26:49,910 --> 00:26:53,230
I have discussed in an earlier lecture
我在之前的一讲中讨论过，

510
00:26:54,670 --> 00:26:57,110
and the biological safety cabinet is designed
生物安全柜的设计目的

511
00:26:57,110 --> 00:27:02,630
to protect the laboratory user from aerosols.
是保护实验室使用者免受气溶胶危害。

512
00:27:02,630 --> 00:27:05,510
These are processes which generate aerosols.
这些是会产生气溶胶的操作。

513
00:27:05,510 --> 00:27:09,430
For instance, a simple pipetting procedure
例如，一个简单的移液操作

514
00:27:09,430 --> 00:27:10,630
may generate an aerosol.
就可能产生气溶胶。

515
00:27:10,630 --> 00:27:13,710
Pipetting onto a slide can generate an aerosol
往载玻片上移液会产生气溶胶，

516
00:27:14,510 --> 00:27:18,070
and centrifugation can also generate aerosols.
离心也会产生气溶胶。

517
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:22,630
Now this kind of centrifuge must preferably not be used
这种离心机最好不要

518
00:27:22,630 --> 00:27:27,310
in biological safety level three and four facility
在生物安全三级和四级设施中使用，

519
00:27:28,830 --> 00:27:31,910
as the rotor is a potential source
因为当你打开转子时，

520
00:27:31,910 --> 00:27:35,330
of the biological agent when you open it.
它可能成为生物因子的来源。

521
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:39,790
Now what happens in centrifuge is that your liquid
离心机中发生的情况是，你的液体

522
00:27:39,790 --> 00:27:44,270
or your fluids are spun at very high RPMs,
或流体以非常高的转速旋转，

